# Security

Follow `instructions/security.md` whenever the change touches HTTP, auth, data access, logging, uploads, or configuration. For local/remote env and `.env` workflow, also follow `instructions/environment.md`.

- Validate strictly; whitelist fields; reject unexpected input.
- Keep errors safe; never leak stack traces or secrets to clients.
- Never log secrets, tokens, cookies, OTPs, passwords, or authorization headers.
- Treat authentication and authorization separately; enforce ownership server-side.
- Authorization fails closed; check permissions, never role names. See `instructions/authorization.md`.
- Derive owner scope from the authenticated principal, never from client-supplied ids.
- Never commit secrets or put credentials in AI host config directories.
- Never invent credentials or copy production database/Redis secrets into development config.
